/* Host-side validation of the embodiOS hand-assembled SPIR-V compute shaders.
 *
 * Runs kernel/ai/vk_shaders.h (generated by tools/spirv_gen.py) on the
 * lavapipe software Vulkan driver and compares against a CPU reference that
 * reuses the kernel's own dequant math (fp16->fp32 from
 * kernel/ai/gguf_inference.c).
 *
 * Build (from repo root):
 *     cc -O2 -Wall tools/host_test_vulkan.c -o tools/host_test_vulkan \
 *        -l:libvulkan.so.1 -lm
 * or simply:
 *     make -C tools vktest
 *
 * Run:
 *     tools/host_test_vulkan
 * (lavapipe is selected automatically via VK_ICD_FILENAMES unless the caller
 * already configured an ICD.)
 *
 * Pass criteria:
 *   matmul_f32 : max abs error < 1e-3  (identical accumulation order, so the
 *                expected value is actually ~0)
 *   matmul_q8_0: max relative error < 1e-2 (per-block dequant structure
 *                matches the kernel scalar dot product)
 */

